1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,158
Let us recap.

2
00:00:01,158 --> 00:00:10,156
Every electrode has a potential, measured as a reduction potential against the standard hydrogen electrode, or in practice against calomel.

3
00:00:10,156 --> 00:00:14,726
The electrochemical series ranks reducing and oxidising power.

4
00:00:14,726 --> 00:00:24,231
In a voltaic cell, oxidation happens at the negative anode, reduction at the positive cathode, and a salt bridge closes the circuit.

5
00:00:24,231 --> 00:00:29,570
E nought cell is cathode minus anode, corrected by the Nernst equation.

6
00:00:29,570 --> 00:00:40,078
Delta G is minus n F E, which links cell potential to the equilibrium constant, and one faraday deposits one gram equivalent.

7
00:00:40,078 --> 00:00:44,075
And batteries and fuel cells put all of it to work.

